74.text:
 One JSON object per line: {"flow":"01J9…","dir":"request","kind":"head","seq":0,"head":{"headers":[["content-type","application/json"]],"method":"POST","url":"https://api.example.com/v1/x"}}
{"flow":"01J9…","dir":"request","kind":"data","seq":1,"data":"aGVsbG8="}
{"flow":"01J9…","dir":"request","kind":"end","seq":2,"bytes":5} field meaning flow the exchange's id in the flow log dir request or response kind head, data (body bytes, base64), truncated (max_capture_body_bytes reached; nothing more is recorded) or end (with the total bytes, and aborted: true if the body did not complete) seq the record's position for this flow and direction A body is its data records joined in seq order. Each data record
holds at most 48 KiB of body, so lines stay under 64 KiB plus a little
JSON, apart from head lines, which can be up to limits.max_header_bytes.

105.text:
 POST /roxy/v1/enrol with the enrolment token. {
  "roxy_version": "0.1.0",
  "protocol_version": 1
} field meaning roxy_version the node's roxy version protocol_version 1 {
  "node_id": "node-7f3a9c",
  "token": "nt1-9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",
  "not_after": "2026-11-05T10:12:00Z",
  "renew_after_seconds": 1296000
} field meaning node_id chosen by the server: 1 to 128 characters from A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ -, fixed for the life of the node token the node token: 1 to 512 characters valid in a bearer token. The node stores it and sends it unchanged not_after when the server stops accepting the token, in UTC renew_after_seconds when the node should renew the token, counted from when it received it. The node renews no later than two thirds of the way to not_after whatever this says The control plane decides how long tokens last and how it stores them.
We recommend single-use enrolment tokens with a short expiry, and storing
node tokens hashed. The node keeps its token in its state dir (mode
0600).

107.text:
 POST /roxy/v1/lease with the node token. The body reports the node's
state: {
  "lease_id": "lease-01J9Z8K3",
  "roxy_version": "0.1.0",
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "uptime_seconds": 86400,
  "policy_state": "loaded",
  "spooled_bytes": 0,
  "seq_unreserved": false,
  "quarantine": null
} field meaning lease_id the lease the node has applied, or null before the first. A node that reports an old lease_id did not apply the latest lease policy_state none (no lease yet), loaded or expired spooled_bytes flow-log data waiting to be acknowledged seq_unreserved true if the node cannot save its flow sequence counter, so a restart might reuse sequence numbers. A node that reports this for long needs its state dir looked at quarantine the node's quarantine, or null {
  "id": "q-01J9ZB7QX4R2M8K3N5P6T7V8W9",
  "since": "2026-10-13T09:14:02Z",
  "cause": {"kind": "rule", "rule": "exfil-guard", "flow": "01J9ZB7P"}
} field meaning id the incident's id, which a release must name since when it was tripped, by the node's clock cause what tripped it: kind: rule with the rule and flow, kind: threshold with the listener and its threshold, or kind: layer with the layer and flow The server answers 200 with the whole lease on every poll, or an
error.

108.text:
 {
  "lease_id": "lease-01J9Z8K3",
  "valid_for_seconds": 900,
  "refresh_after_seconds": 300,
  "config": "version: 1\nlisteners:\n  - name: proxy\n    bind: 0.0.0.0:8080\nsecrets:\n  github: { lease: true }\nrules:\n  - id: github\n    when: host == \"api.github.com\"\n    then: [allow]\n",
  "secrets": {
    "github": "ghp_example"
  },
  "state_epoch": "2026-10-06T09:00:00Z",
  "flow": {
    "ship": true,
    "batch_max_bytes": 1048576,
    "flush_interval_seconds": 5,
    "spool_high_water_bytes": 67108864,
    "on_high_water": "hold"
  },
  "quarantine": {
    "release": ["q-01J9ZB7QX4R2M8K3N5P6T7V8W9"]
  }
} field meaning lease_id any string that changes whenever anything else in the lease changes valid_for_seconds how long the lease is valid, measured by the node's own clock from just before it sent the request. Clock differences between the node and server do not matter refresh_after_seconds when to poll next. Leave room for several retries; a third of valid_for_seconds is reasonable. The node polls no later than halfway through the lease config a complete roxy.yaml. Secrets the lease supplies are declared as name: { lease: true } secrets the value of each lease: true secret state_epoch any string. When it changes, the node clears all rule state and metric counts before applying the lease, which is how a control plane lifts a lockout a rule imposed flow how to send the flow log (flow upload). ship: false turns it off. on_high_water says what happens when spool_high_water_bytes are waiting: hold holds traffic, spool drops the oldest events quarantine optional. release lists the quarantine ids the control plane has released. The node lifts its quarantine when its id is listed interception_ca reserved; not sent by a v1 server The node applies a lease in full or not at all. A lease whose config
roxy check would reject, or that lacks a secret the config declares, is
logged and ignored, and the node keeps the lease it has. A change to
secrets alone is applied without reloading the rest of the policy.
